This was my first wizard ascension, after months and
months of trying.  Thanks to the people who replied in
my "tips for early-game wizards" thread, you guys really
helped a lot!  Wizards really are as awesome as I thought
they would be. :) (though a bit wimpy on the Planes --
maybe AC -29 was too high?).

I started as a gnomish wizard so the Mines would be
easier.  I was lucky in that I started with a wand of fire
and found a spellbook of identify on T1116.  With my +ID
and gauntlets of power, I was happy to wear metal armor
and throw daggers until well into the game (as was
suggested).  Minetown was crossaligned and not very
useful to me (only found 4 candles). I found a +5 pair
of iron shoes in Sokoban, which I rustproofed and wore
until I found speed boots (which was really late).

I genocided eels (revenge!) and sacrificed for Magicbane
at the first opportunity.  (Spells of create monster made
this much easier.)  After getting my strength to 18, I
ditched my gauntlets of power for +2 leather gloves.
At some point I also genocided L and disenchanters, but
eels were definitely first priority. =P

I did the castle before the quest (which I probably shouldn't
have done given I didn't have fire resistance and had to go
upstairs once to heal).  The wand of wishing was at 0:3 and
gave me +2 SDSM, +magic mapping, =oC, and 7 candles
at various stages in the game.  Magic mapping let me get
through Gehennom in 6000 turns (from entering the gate
to performing the invocation), which was Pretty Damn Sweet.

The quest was easy.  I instakilled the Dark One with
a wand of death I'd found at the castle, so I never got to
find out how bad he was.  The throne at the entry level
gave me a wish, which I used on a +3 HoB.

The sanctum and planes were harsh.  I think I would
have died several times over had I not wished for the ring
of conflict (and found two more rings of conflict on the
ground upon entering the Sanctum -- such is life).  The
high priest (who I burned a !oFH on) took off 40 HP in one
hit. The Plane of Air nearly killed me -- I was engulfed three
times, and wands of teleportation always seemed to teleport
air elementals one square away.  I had a gremlin infestation
on the Plane of Water, so I used my last blessed genocide
scroll to nuke g (while confused!).  I brought a helm of
opposite alignment to Astral but decided not to use it at
the last minute (my god was nice to me, he gave me
Magicbane =P).  The second altar (Death's) was the right
one.

I found and wore an amulet of life saving early on.  20000
turns later, I discovered it was missing and suspected a
nymph had taken it.  Upon quaffing a potion of enlightenment
and reviewing my ttyrecs, I discovered a cobra had bit
me to death while fainting from hunger, and I didn't notice
because I was skipping messages. (How the hell do you
not notice *dying*?!)  My second AoLS was spent in
Vlad's tower (and involved a nurse-leocrotta combo).

